voc.txt was generated from a dump of the Latvian Wikipedia like so:

scripts/wikipedia-dump-to-freq lvwiki-20261101-pages-articles.xml.bz2 5 '[a-z\x{101}\x{10D}\x{113}\x{123}\x{12B}\x{137}\x{13C}\x{146}\x{161}\x{16B}\x{17E}]' > voc.freq
scripts/freq-to-voc 10 < voc.freq > latvian/voc.txt

The dump used was dated 2026-11-01.

The letter class is the lower case Latvian alphabet plus q, w, x and y, so
capitalised words and words containing other letters are not counted.  Only
words which occur at least 10 times are kept.

output.txt was generated from voc.txt by running it through the stemmer:

stemwords -l latvian -c UTF_8 -i latvian/voc.txt -o latvian/output.txt

